/-!
# Checked-definition execution through an actual finite source program

The actual compiler, closed directed reductions, public source query and
whole-frontier controller agree on reachable data-value observations. The
selected recursive row class joins the qualified descriptor execution and
retains its dependent result type. Closed-machine normalization is proved
separately from answer correspondence.

Checked ground dependencies transport normalization through actual source
configurations and the public bind to the whole-frontier controller. The
full compiler supplies its dependency licence, and actual directed-source
normalization transports through this complete execution chain.

The general normal-form scanner returns its marker exactly for native
normal forms, at every native scope and under all twelve term constructors.
Its actual source query terminates for every scoped native input. Public
source and frontier answers are exactly the reachable directed native normal
forms, including functions and dependent type formers. Native directed
accessibility gives termination of the actual public source and controller.
Typing is preserved under an exact package's preservation licence, or for
old terms through the qualified vector package. A concrete declaration passes
the structural compiler gate while its typing check refuses it, so arbitrary
new-definition qualification is not inferred. These results retain actual
continuations, stores and bags; equivalence of result multiplicities and
equivalence under arbitrary surrounding programs remain separate obligations.

Verdict-compiled calls earn their old-term support licence from actual typing
and fresh declarations. Their general normal answers agree with the qualified
descriptor execution, and base directed accessibility reaches the actual
source and controller. A checked append call retains its dependent result
even in a development with an unrelated typing-refused raw row. Raw named-row
preservation and qualification of those extensions remain separate obligations.
-/
